.TH "RAPTOR-HISTORY" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-history \- list, snapshot or restore saved versions of a model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor history\fR [\-h] [\-\-snapshot] [\-\-label TEXT] [\-\-description TEXT] [\-\-description\-file PATH] [\-\-describe SNAPSHOT] [\-\-restore SNAPSHOT] [\-o PATH] [\-\-force] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version history kept by the desktop application on save. Snapshots live in the user's private state folder, not beside the model.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR
record the file as it is now
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fITEXT\fR
label the snapshot (with \-\-snapshot); an unchanged file re\-labels its newest version
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR
Markdown description for the snapshot (with \-\-snapshot), or with \-\-describe for that version
.TP
\fB\-\-description\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
read the Markdown description from a file ('\-' is standard input)
.TP
\fB\-\-describe\fR \fISNAPSHOT\fR
set (or with an empty description, clear) the description of an existing snapshot
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fISNAPSHOT\fR
write this snapshot to \-\-output (or \-\-force over MODEL)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
destination for \-\-restore
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
allow \-\-restore to overwrite MODEL or an existing \-\-output
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
